fore conditions are checked"},{"path":"reference/pokemon-essentials/Data/Scripts/014_Pokemon/005_Pokemon_Owner.rb","lines":[19,25],"unit":"four constructor fields submitted together, then assigned unchanged"},{"path":"reference/pokemon-essentials/Data/Scripts/014_Pokemon/005_Pokemon_Owner.rb","lines":[45,65],"unit":"individual field setters submit one type condition and reject numeric name"},{"path":"reference/pokemon-essentials/Data/Scripts/014_Pokemon/001_Pokemon.rb","lines":[1198,1205],"unit":"an existing owner record is accepted as-is; no recursive field validation"}],"formal":[{"path":"deliverables/final-specification-set/creature-rpg/wp18-creature-identity-species-ownership.md","lines":[247,254],"clause":"§6.1 four field types and constructor/setter type validation"},{"path":"deliverables/final-specification-set/creature-rpg/wp18-creature-identity-species-ownership.md","lines":[346,346],"clause":"§9 states owner constructor mismatched field types report error without equality exception"},{"path":"deliverables/final-specification-set/test-catalog/creature-rpg-wp18-20-24-25-26.md","lines":[5,36],"clause":"CI-01–28 no constructor same-value type-bypass contrast"}],"prerequisites":["Unmodified reference constructor and generic validator; bare direct owner constructor, not PBS input or a normal user name dialog.","Inputs are bounded ordinary integers or ordinary text; no custom equality/hash behavior.","No plugin wrappers or extra schema validation.","Other constructor fields are integers and dependencies for type validation are present."],"comparison":"The formal failure clause says a constructor field type mismatch raises an error. Source groups type conditions by argument value; equal values keep the later condition. A numeric name equal to later integer gender/language therefore loses its text requirement and is stored as an integer. The individual name setter still rejects numeric input because its single check cannot be masked.","minimal_counterexample":{"constructor_inputs":{"id":0,"name":0,"gender":0,"language":2},"source_result":{"constructed":true,"stored_name":0,"stored_name_type":"Integer"},"formal_assertion_result":"report error for non-string name","contrasts":[{"input":[1,0,0,2],"result":"constructs integer name0"},{"input":[1,0,1,2],"result":"ArgumentError; name0 does not merge with later integer fields"},{"input":[0,"Valid",0,2],"result":"constructs legal string name"},{"action":"set name0 on legal owner","result":"ArgumentError; prior name preserved"}]},"cancel_exception_partial_commit":"No interactive cancellation here. Rejected constructor input fails before all four field writes; accepted colliding input writes all four values unchanged. Individual name-setter rejection occurs before name mutation. No game/save execution or new transaction guarantee is asserted. Existing owner input in creature creation is accepted as the owner record; malformed internal name is not recursively rejected there.","negative_search":{"log":"logs/owner-validation-search.json","scope":"WP18 full text and complete associated test catalog, WP03 full text plus focused diagnostic text search; source validator and owner file fully read","result":"No clause or CI test records equal constructor argument values masking the name type condition. Negative search alone is not a full-domain absence claim."},"necessary_consumers":"Full core creature creation was read; explicit owner object branch preserves object. All owner constructors and field writers plus full generic validation function were read. Host UI/dynamic authors/real saves were not run.","impact":"Incorrect static failure requirement and cross-field type invariant at the author-facing constructor boundary; a later clean-room validator that checks every field will behave differently on this reference counterexample. This does not require preserving malformed-name acceptance in the future product.","minimal_repair":"Limit unconditional rejection to individual field writers and constructor cases whose name condition remains checked. Record the bounded direct-constructor same-value counterexample as reference behavior: integer name0 with gender0 is accepted and stored; name0 with gender1 is rejected; later setter name0 is rejected. Keep valid field types as expected domain input and explicitly distinguish reference exception from future design.","preserve_scope":["No future validation container/API recommendation","No source fragments in specifications","No requirement to reproduce malformed acceptance in the future","Valid constructor and language/default behavior unchanged","No claim about PBS or normal UI validation bypass"],"synchronize":["WP18 §6.1 and §9 failure clause","CI static constructor/setter equality contrast","Any cross-spec claim of all owner fields always satisfying types, if present"],"acceptance_regression":["direct inputs[0,0,0,2] accepted with integer name0","direct inputs[1,0,1,2] rejected before fields assign","legal string name remains accepted","single name write0 rejected and existing name preserved","valid language identity/default semantics unchanged"],"validation":{"kind":"ISOLATED_REFERENCE_EXECUTION","script":"isolated-owner-validation.rb","log":"logs/owner-validation.json","method":"Loaded previously fully inspected validator/owner definitions in isolated local Ruby2.6. No game/RGSS/real save/IO mutation. Direct original constructor and name setter executed.","observed":"Two numeric-name colliding inputs accepted; noncolliding constructor and setter rejected.","not_executed":["Full game creature creation with malformed owner","Native UI","Real save"],"observation_class":"REFERENCE_OBSERVATION_WITH_SURROGATES","native_game_execution_count":0,"native_UI_execution_count":0,"real_save_execution_count":0,"independent_model_execution_count":0,"shell_pipeline_exit_code":0,"ruby_process_exit_code":"NOT_CAPTURED_SEPARATELY; shell pipeline reports tee status","actual_UTC_execution_time":"NOT_CAPTURED_AT_EXECUTION; not re